{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Moses will speak and the Elohim will answer him with a voice</b> — They said in the Mekhilta (here) that this refers to the hour of the giving of the Torah, that Moses was making the utterances heard to Israel, as Rashi wrote (Rashi on Exodus 19:19). But according to the way of the peshat, he does not speak in this manner yet; rather, HaShem the glorious descended upon the mountain on the third day, and Moses brought the people out from the camp to meet the Glory that appeared to them, <b>and they stationed themselves</b> at <b>the foot of the mountain</b>, while Moses went up above, near the top of the mountain where the Glory was, and He encamps for Himself and speaks with Israel to instruct them what they should do. And Israel hears the voice of Elohim answering him and commanding us, but they will not understand what He says to him. And He commands him with the commandments stated afterwards in the pericope: <b>Go down, warn the people</b>, etc.; <b>Go, descend, and you shall ascend, you and Aaron with you</b>, etc. And this was before the giving of the Torah and also at the hour of the utterances, for Moses did not ascend to the top of the mountain, <b>into the thick cloud where the Elohim was</b>, until after the giving of the Torah. And thus He said (Deuteronomy 5:5): \"I stood between YHWH and you at that time, to declare to you the word of YHWH, for you feared the fire and did not ascend the mountain, saying\" — as I ascended. And there are commentators who explain that Israel were exceedingly afraid from the sound of the shofar that went and grew exceedingly strong (Exodus 19:19), and Moses would say first: direct your minds, for now you will hear a voice in such a manner, and immediately the Elohim will answer him with that same voice."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The abbreviation אח\"כ is resolved as אחר כך ('afterwards'); the phrase הכבוד מחצה לעצמו is translated hyper-literally as 'the Glory encamps for Himself,' though the sense may carry an additional nuance of establishing a boundary."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:11:07.949205255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}